SWEET WLAN open-network join (patch 0400, oriole upstream port Step 10; user 2026-11-19: join an open campus guest network at boot). Upstream's boot join is WPA2-PSK only: the WLANCRED blob refuses any
security word but 0, L24 sends wpa_auth WPA2_AUTH_PSK / wsec AES, L25 needs a PMK, the target's RSNE and a finished host 4-way before the en0 hand-over.
(a) sweet_wlan_cred.h: security word 1 = open (tools/mkwlancred.py PIXOS_WIFI*_SECURITY=open): psk_len 0, psk bytes zero, no PMK; swc_creds.open; line `credentials loaded security=open`. Every other word stays refused.
(b) sweet_wlan_join_fw.h: swj_join_cmds_open = the six H1..H5 commands with wpa_auth 0 and wsec 0 (sup_wpa 0, auth 0 open system, mfp 0 and the v1 join unchanged) [src OpenBSD sys/dev/ic/bwfm.c:2036-2040, the
    no-privacy branch of bwfm_connect: BWFM_WPA_AUTH_DISABLED, BWFM_WSEC_NONE, BWFM_AUTH_OPEN; bwfmreg.h:167, 180, 188 = 0]. sweet_wlan.c uses it when swc_creds.open.
(c) L25 (sweet_wlan_l25.h cfg.open, sweet_wlan_l25_rsne.h tgt.open, sweet_wlan_l25_glue.h, sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h): no PMK is required; the target record must carry NO RSNE (one with an RSNE is refused:
    the credentials say open); a zero cfg BSSID adopts the record (rsne_len 0); swl25_go skips the supplicant context and the 4-way, sets hs_done (the en0 hand-over's check) and prints `L25 done: open network (no keys)`.
(d) Keep mode: the 0282 re-join is not armed for an open link (GAP: stays DOWN after an AP loss); the Apple80211 kept link answers sec=open (no privacy bit, Get 2 auth lower 1 / upper 0 [guess from the observed
    WPA2-PSK pair lower 1 / upper 8]).
No new register, address, store kind or ioctl: the L24 SET_VARs are the same names with value 0 (the L24 list whitelists the built payloads exactly), L25 makes fewer calls. WPA2-PSK blobs take the old path byte for byte.
Host test: shim/wlan_open_host_test.c (the cred + join_fw hunks of this patch on the 0206 headers: open blob load, refusals, the open join payloads). ORDER: after 0399.
